# Normalize line endings across platforms. Text files are LF in the index and LF
# on checkout everywhere, Windows included. `eol=lf` is an explicit per-path
# setting, so it overrides whatever `core.autocrlf` a contributor happens to
# have, and Git for Windows sets `core.autocrlf=true` at system scope by
# default. Nobody has to unset anything: a fresh clone is LF on disk regardless.
#
# `text=auto` covers the other direction, normalizing CRLF back to LF on the way
# into the index. That is why a tool that rewrites a tracked file with CRLF
# after checkout leaves `git status` and `git diff` clean and nothing reports the
# drift. Only `git ls-files --eol` sees it; CONTRIBUTING.md carries the check.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Be explicit about the file kinds this kit ships.
*.py    text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.tmpl  text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.mdc   text eol=lf

# Anything binary that lands later stays untouched.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.gif   binary
*.pdf   binary
